  "note": "Corrects the parser's ambiguous-heading guess on the \"Herbs\" heading (revid 15285801): its 8 rows (Grimy avantoe 1/64.6, Grimy kwuarm 1/64.6, Grimy ranarr weed 1/80.8, Grimy snapdragon 1/80.8, Grimy cadantine 1/80.8, Grimy dwarf weed 1/80.8, Grimy lantadyme 1/107.7, Grimy torstol 1/107.7) carry no Pre-roll/Tertiary/Secondary keyword, so build-tables.ts's final fallback flagged it needs_review and defaulted to a preroll guess. Checked directly against https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Alchemical_Hydra: the section's own prose states \"There is a 10/101 chance to get noted herbs\", and the wiki's #vardefine/#expr source computes each row as 1/(multiplier*herbbase) with herbbase = 10/101/32 and multipliers 5,5,4,4,4,4,3,3 (summing to 32) \u2014 the exact same access-rate-partition shape as this boss's own \"Seeds\" heading two sections below, which the parser already resolves automatically into a single `oneOf` node at its declared access rate because that heading's rows come from a recognised template transclusion (TreeHerbSeedDropLines) carrying a declared access rate. \"Herbs\" fails that same auto-detection only because it is written as inline #vardefine/#expr wikitext rather than a transclusion \u2014 not because the underlying mechanic differs. Replaces only that heading's shape, preroll (8 independently-triggered entries) -> independent (a single oneOf partitioning the 10/101 access roll), matching the Seeds table's already-verified pattern; other non-unique tables are unchanged from the generated document. Also corrects the Unique pre-roll chain using the same revision's prose and exact conditional denominators: thrownaxe 2000, knife 2000, claw 1000, tail 512, leather 512, ring piece 180. The displayed ~1/181.1 rate is for any ring piece after earlier failures, not each component. The brimstone_ring footnote specifies eye, fang, heart order. A shared ordered preroll with resetPerSet ownership gates enforce that order for every complete set without source-specific simulator logic.",
